1. General Guidelines
Language:

Backend: JavaScript (Node.js, ES modules)

Frontend: JavaScript + JSX (React.js), no TypeScript

Frameworks/Libraries:

Backend: Node.js + Express.js, Socket.IO (or ws), KafkaJS for Kafka integration

Frontend: React.js, D3.js (or vis.js) for graph visualization, Redux Toolkit or Zustand for state management

Structure: Follow a modular, feature-based folder structure (backend & frontend separated).

Style: Clean, well-commented code. Consistent naming conventions (camelCase for vars/functions, PascalCase for components).

Version Control: Assume Git is used with .gitignore set for node_modules, build outputs, .env.

